  "message": "Sure thing! Here’s a quick refresher on the finance‑analysis crew I coordinate:\n\n| Agent / Role | What it does | Typical focus |\n|--------------|--------------|----------------|\n| **mapper_cash** | Scans the expense database for vendor patterns paid **in cash** (method = “CASH”). | Finds cash‑purchase merchants, flags recurring cash spend, builds the cash‑monthly‑totals report. |\n| **mapper_card** | Looks for transactions made with **card swipes** (method = “CARD”). | Generates the card‑monthly‑totals, highlights new card merchants and any odd spikes. |\n| **mapper_bank** | Handles ACH, online‑transfer and other **bank‑based payments** (method = “BANK”). | Produces the bank‑monthly‑totals and spots recurring bills that come directly from the bank. |\n| **mapper_other** | Catches everything else – paper checks, misc or uncategorized items (method = “OTHER”). | Supplies the “other‑monthly‑totals” and helps catch stray or mis‑tagged expenses. |\n| **synthesizer** | Merges the four mapper reports and flags missed bills, amount anomalies, and new recurring candidates. | Outputs the synthesis_report.html and a summary of anything that looks off. |\n| **receipt_scanner** | Scans uploaded receipt images, matches them to expense rows, and finds orphaned or mislabeled receipts. | Generates the orphaned‑receipts report and keeps receipt‑expense linkage clean. |\n| **expense_reconciler** | Looks for expense rows without a matching receipt (excluding known receipt‑less transactions). | Produces the unaccounted‑expenses_report.md. |\n| **progress_check** | Read‑only status tool that tells you which reports already exist, their timestamps, and whether anything is stale. | Gives a quick health‑check without running any heavy analysis. |\n\nThese “people” (actually specialized agents) work together to map cash, card, bank, and other transactions, scan receipts, reconcile expenses, and synthesize everything into clear, up‑to‑date reports. Let me know if you’d like more details on any of them or want to run a specific analysis!",
